---
// The page-level attribution surface. Markup and styles only; it has no logic
// to put anywhere else. See docs/spec/attribution-surface.md.
---

<!--
  Bottom-left, and it stays there at every viewport.

  The page has four corners and three are spoken for: the header owns top-left,
  the desktop card owns bottom-right, and on a phone the full-bleed sheet owns
  the whole bottom edge whenever a card is open. Measured rather than argued —
  top-right lands 3211px² on the header caption at 375px, and bottom-left is
  100% behind the sheet on both phone viewports with a card open.

  ⚠️ The sheet occlusion is **accepted, not fixed**: occluded by a dismissible,
  non-modal overlay is not the same as conditionally rendered — the element is in
  the DOM and displayed on load, and the sheet is one gesture from dismissal. The
  alternative (re-homing into the header lockup below the breakpoint) is clear
  everywhere and costs a DOM re-home rather than a media query, which would give
  `(max-width: 700px), (max-height: 500px)` a **third** holder.
-->
<div class="pattr">
  <!--
    ⚠️ Placeholder for `books.google.com/googlebooks/images/poweredby.png`, at
    the assumed 144x26 footprint every width in the spec inherits. The real image
    is vendored rather than hotlinked — this page makes **zero** third-party
    requests today, and a hotlinked PNG would disclose every visitor's IP and
    referer to Google on a `noindex` site, to satisfy an obligation that has
    nothing to do with privacy. The file is not in the repo yet; fetching
    third-party artwork is the owner's call.
  -->
  <span class="pattr-mark" role="img" aria-label="powered by Google">powered by Google</span>
  <!--
    The first page chrome on this site that is not inert. The surface sets itself
    `pointer-events: none` so drag-to-look-around passes straight through it; the
    anchor has to opt back out.
  -->
  <a class="pattr-link" href="/attribution">Attribution</a>
</div>

<style>
  .pattr {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    left: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    /* Above the shelf, below the card and the debug surfaces. */
    z-index: 5;
    /* Inert by default — the shelf is dragged through this corner. */
    pointer-events: none;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #6f6051;
  }

  .pattr-mark {
    display: inline-block;
    /* The assumed footprint of Google's powered-by image. */
    width: 144px;
    height: 26px;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.4rem;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(242, 232, 220, 0.18);
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    line-height: 1;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .pattr-link {
    /*
      44px, and it is the height of the whole row: WCAG 2.5.5's touch target,
      not the graphic, is what sets it — so shrinking the graphic buys width and
      nothing else.
    */
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0 0.25rem;
    color: #857361;
    /* The one thing here that is not inert. */
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  .pattr-link:hover,
  .pattr-link:focus-visible {
    color: #c9b8a4;
  }
</style>
